{"duration_api_ms":144851,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":1.0308283999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":48,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51354,"cache_read_input_tokens":1569722,"output_tokens":15293,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2850},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51354,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1451,"cache_read_input_tokens":83065,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":48,"outputTokens":15293,"cacheReadInputTokens":1569722,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51354,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0308283999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2850,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":51354,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0041 is measured and committed (`53ee44e`), but the numbers are not in `baseline.md` as the Goal asked: that file is outside this packet's target. I put them in `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0041-x2t-pdf-split.md` and requested a follow-up packet to copy them over. The packet has no acceptance commands, so there was nothing to run; `theseus validate` reports 0 errors.\n\n**Where the time goes** (native 9.3.7-1 package, median of 3 runs, traced with strace):\n\n| Run | Total | Start + V8 init | Loading the JS editor code | Layout (JS) | Writing the output |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Empty docx → pdf | 0.84 s | ~55 ms | 333 ms | 413 ms | 22 ms |\n| Empty xlsx → pdf | 0.68 s | ~56 ms | 330 ms | 267 ms | 17 ms |\n| Empty pptx → pdf | 1.21 s | ~67 ms | 330 ms | 682 ms | 27 ms |\n| 300-page docx → pdf | 11.9 s | 64 ms | 330 ms | 7.5 s | 2.9 s |\n| 50k-row xlsx → pdf | 50.2 s | 84 ms | 349 ms | 44.3 s | 4.3 s |\n| 80-slide pptx → pdf | 5.9 s | 67 ms | 370 ms | 3.4 s | 1.3 s |\n| Save, empty doc → docx | 0.93 s | 72 ms | 331 ms | 495 ms | 60 ms |\n| Save, 300-page doc → docx | 4.0 s | 55 ms | 369 ms | 2.3 s | 1.1 s |\n\n- **Small documents:** the cost is fixed and almost all JavaScript. Loading the editor code takes about 330 ms on every run, and the first layout pass adds 270–680 ms even for an empty file. Process start plus V8 setup is only about 60 ms, and writing the PDF about 20 ms.\n- **Large documents:** layout takes 63–88% of the time, the writer 9–24%, and reading the source file 3–5%.\n- **Worst case:** the 50k-row spreadsheet to PDF takes about 50 s, 44 s of it in layout.\n- **Code cache:** the package ships a V8 code cache (`sdk-all.cache`) for each editor, but no startup snapshot. Without the cache a run is about 400 ms slower, and x2t silently rebuilds it as whichever user runs it. I removed it for that test and put the original back.\n- **strace overhead:** tracing adds about 10–20%. Untraced, the empty docx takes 0.62–0.72 s and the 300-page docx 9.6 s.\n\n**Decisions**\n- **Save with no edits:** the save conversion was measured with an empty change list, because the database holds no real changes. It shows the fixed cost of a save, not the cost of applying edits.\n- **New script:** the files from attempt 1 were not in this worktree, so I rewrote the measurement script: `.theseus/oracle/perf/x2t-split.sh`.\n\n**Follow-up requests** (in `.theseus/spawn/`, waiting for the factory's approval):\n1. Copy the table and conclusion into `baseline.md`.\n2. Investigate why spreadsheet → PDF layout is so slow (needs `documentserver`).\n\nThe Executor log, the Lessons section and the friction line are filled in.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- **Fixed cost:** x2t's PDF and save time is in the JavaScript renderer, not in x2t's C++ code. A renderer process kept alive between conversions would cut both the 0.33 s code load and the first-layout warm-up. A V8 startup snapshot would only cut the code load.\n- **Code cache:** `sdk-all.cache` is already a V8 code cache (it saves about 0.4 s), and x2t regenerates it silently if it is missing.\n- **Phase markers:** tracing file opens is enough to split phases: `DoctRenderer.config`, `sdk-all-min.js`, `AllFonts.js` and `font_selection.bin` each mark a boundary.","ttft_ms":1930,"type":"result","duration_ms":415465,"uuid":"52460a90-0d72-4303-a3be-e84e56ac35eb","ttft_stream_ms":845,"time_to_request_ms":235,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":106,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":19,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":24,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":37,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":162,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":134,"process_rss_mib_result":244,"process_anon_mib_result":149,"process_peak_rss_mib":274,"process_cpu_ms_turn":6462,"process_wall_ms_turn":415461,"process_cpu_ms_s